# What is NOT shipped in the .vsix. The published extension is the bundle, the panel assets and
# the documents a reviewer needs — nothing that would let source drift from what runs.
.github/**
.vscode/**
src/**
tests/**
scripts/**
dist-tests/**
# The integration harness runs the extension inside a real VS Code. It has no business inside the
# extension the user installs: it is test code, it is dead weight in the download, and shipping the
# runner alongside the product is how a test fixture ends up looking like a feature.
dist-integration/**
node_modules/**
docs/screenshots/**
# Screenshots belong to the README on GitHub, not in the installed package (vsce rewrites the
# relative links to the repository when publishing).
docs/images/**
**/*.map
tsconfig.json
esbuild.mjs
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml
**/*.ts
# The evaluation report's arithmetic, bundled for `scripts/evaluate.mjs` alone. Nothing the
# extension or the terminal client runs imports it, so shipping it would be dead weight in the
# download — the same mistake as the stale bundle this file's header describes, one order smaller.
dist/eval-report.mjs
# And the bench itself: forty broken repositories, their reference solutions and whatever results a
# run left behind. It is `.gitignore`d, which is not the same as excluded from the package — vsce
# packages what is on disk. It was 156 files and 57 KB of the download, and it is test material: the
# same argument as `dist-integration/**` above, and the same mistake one directory along.
eval/**
